AB  - The proceedings contain 28 papers. The topics discussed include: SC-Bench: a large-scale dataset for smart contract auditing; deriving coding-specific sub-models from LLMs using resource-efficient pruning; RepairBench: leaderboard of frontier models for program repair; with a little help from my (LLM) friends: enhancing static analysis with LLMs to detect software vulnerabilities; automating the detection of code vulnerabilities by analyzing GitHub issues; from zero to sixty at the speed of RAG: improving YAML recipe generation via retrieval; SC-Bench: a large-scale dataset for smart contract auditing; training LLMs for generating IEC 61131-3 structured text with online feedback; and LLM-ProS: analyzing large language models' performance in competitive problem solving.
