TY  - CONF
TI  - AI Enhanced Code Fault Detection and Automated Fixing
DO  - 10.1109/IC-ICNS68863.2026.11537941
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105042243188?origin=resultslist
AB  - Software development can be characterized by complex programs, which can carry with them, syntactic errors and logical bugs, therefore debugging becomes a very time consuming and a demanding undertaking. Conventional debugging systems are intensive in their utilisation of manual effort and rule-based tools which have some limitations in identifying run-time problems and supplying automatic solutions. We present a new AI-based automated debugging system in this paper that combines dynamic validation and pre-trained large language models with a static code analysis to detect bugs and code fixes efficiently. The system makes use of parsing based on Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) to retrieve the functional level components, create test cases, and also detect possible errors as well as logical inconsistency. Pretrained models include CodeLlama, Mistral 7B, CodeT5, and StarCoder which are used to produce context-aware fixes, and a memory module based on vectors is used to increase efficiency by retrieving similar patterns of past bug-fixes. The system is based on an iterative validation procedure to provide accuracy on generated solutions. The experimental analysis based on similarity-based measurements proves that CodeLlama has the best mark of 91.2, which reflects the competence of the offered method in automated program repair and code optimization assignments. © 2026 IEEE.
