TY  - JOUR
TI  - CRec: A tool for recovering the compilability of OCRed code
DO  - 10.1016/j.softx.2026.102735
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105039654501?origin=resultslist
AB  - Code reuse is a prevalent practice in software development. However, extracting code embedded in images remains a challenge. While optical character recognition (OCR) automates the extraction, it often introduces lexical and syntactic errors. CodeT5-OCRfix, the leading tool for correcting such errors, relies on fine-tuning pre-trained code models, but may not capture diverse error types. To bridge this gap, we present CRec, a tool for fixing lexical and syntactic errors in OCRed code. CRec targets fine-grained errors and complements CodeT5-OCRfix by refining its patches. Our primary goal is to recover the compilability of OCRed code, thereby making the output directly usable for developers. We evaluate CRec on 1597 non-compilable samples. Experimental results show that CRec can enhance CodeT5-OCRfix, by increasing the number of compilable fixes from 465 to 764 and raising the compilable rate from 29.12% to 47.84%. © 2026 The Authors.
